When a module declares the same `var` more than once, rolldown treats the variable as never reassigned, so it can replace a read with the value from a different declaration. This PR treats a repeated `var` declaration as a reassignment.

```js
export var flag = false;
console.log(flag);
var flag = true;
```

Run unbundled, this prints `false`. Before, the bundle prints `true`, because the read becomes `console.log(true)`. After, the read stays `console.log(flag)`.

oxc records `var flag = true` as a second declaration of `flag`, not as a write to it, and the AST scanner looks only at write ref

